/-- perturbedWitness2: the close-out on the error side. There exists an admissible
integer pair (source, response) at both caps that satisfies the coupling exactly and the
floor law perturbed by a per-window deficit of 84162012 (coupling scale: +25248603600), yet stays
under the budget head: sumTo d 123 = 1696000 ≤ 1744063. Together with forcingUnderError2 (which
holds over ALL admissible trajectories for every deficit up to the certificate tolerance),
this brackets the adversarial error tolerance of the geometric mechanism at the anchor. -/
theorem perturbedWitness2 :
    ∃ d c : Nat → Int,
      (∀ n, 30000000 * d (n + 1) = 30000 * d n + 30000000 * c n) ∧
      (∀ n, 30000000 * c (n + 1) + 25248603600 ≥ 28424100 * c n) ∧
      d 0 ≤ 1000000 ∧ c 0 ≤ 39000 ∧
      sumTo d 123 ≤ 1744063 :=
    ⟨Wd2P, Wc2P, hexactW2P, hlowW2P, hd0W2P, hc0W2P,
      by have h := simExact2; omega⟩

